# Make a character and get into the dungeon. Included by six of the eighteen
# files in this directory: dive.keys, dive12.keys, explore.keys, followers.keys,
# marathon.keys and smoke.keys. The header used to claim every other script
# included it, which is wrong; check with
# grep -l "@include chargen.keys" tools/keys/*.keys before relying on it.
#
# The character is a standard male orc barbarian, neutral, worshipping
# whichever god the game offers. Orc barbarian is deliberate: it is the
# hardiest starting combination the game recommends to a new player, so a
# scripted walk survives long enough to be worth watching.
#
# The race, subrace, class and alignment are named, not counted, so a race or
# class added to lib/ cannot make this script build a different character.
# See @choose in src/Wposix.cpp. Run with a fixed seed all the same
# (tools/headless.sh <script> <seed>): the attribute rolls decide which feats
# the game offers, and the two feat picks below are still positional.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
@choose "Orc"
@choose "Orc (Standard)"
@choose "Barbarian"
a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets. The sets have no
        #   names, so this one stays positional.
@choose "Neutral"   # and not Neutral Good or Neutral Evil: a name that
                    #   matches an entry outright beats one that is merely
                    #   a prefix of it.
a       # First feat.  Which feats are offered depends on the attribute
a       # Second feat. rolls, so these two stay counted.

# Skill Manager, twice: once for the class pool and once for the pool that
# follows the choice of god. RIGHT spends a rank on the selected skill and
# stops at the skill's maximum, DOWN moves to the next skill, so three RIGHTs
# per skill spends everything available without needing to know how many
# ranks this character has. Character generation will not let go until the
# pool is empty.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

y       # Do you wish to worship <god>? -- yes

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

# The next keystroke lands in the dungeon, in play mode.
